A||||6||Cheever3000||Water in my trunks||||11||
Z||000000||Cheever3000||09-02-2001||09:14 PM||||Okay, so we have had a full week of torrential rain, but I went to the trunk of my 88GT and saw water standing in there.  If I had been on a trip my luggage would be soaked.  If I had gotten paper instead of plastic I would have a half-gallon of soup.  Is this a common problem?  Is my seal bad?  It looks great, but obviously isn't doing its job.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||09-02-2001||09:44 PM||||Trunk, as in rear compartment, or trunk as in front compartment? <P>If it's the rear, you may have water leaking in through the wing-mounting holes (if you have a wing)... <P>One trick I've used is when the weather is dry, sprinkle baby powder around the outside of the seal, and on the seal, and the next time it rains, see where the water is coming in by tracing the wet baby powder...<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||09-02-2001||09:51 PM||||It is likely cause your rear wheel wells are rotten through, pull out the carpet and inspect for rust.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||09-04-2001||04:01 PM||||My 85gt did the same thing.  I found that one of the luggage rack rubber insert nuts was missing.  This provided a 1/2" diameter hole under the rack.  I got some new ones at AutoZone and fixed it good as new.||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||09-04-2001||04:06 PM||||Spoiler gasket leaking?||||reg||5
Z||000005||Rick 88||09-04-2001||10:45 PM||||Hey you could alway move to El Paso! No rain, no rust, no humidity. Barring that, check you spoiler gaskets, trunk lid adjustment, and trunk gasket. If they check out pull the trunk carpet and look for rust holes,or bad sealer on the seams. Send some rain this way. We could sure use some.<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||12
Z||000006||Cheever3000||09-04-2001||11:55 PM||||Thanks a lot guys.  If I had room in the garage, I could pull in there to try out those ideas.  We're into our second week of rain, and it's s'pozed to continue.  And Friday I need to get the other car (which IS in the garage) ready for Saturday's Bud Classic open car show.  This is the show that was postponed due to the June 9th Allison storm flood.  I wonder if I can reserve some room on my neighbor's ark.<BR>||||reg||1
